[Guidelines 2006 > 2 > 2.7 > 2.7.3 > SCAPC may be justified where;]
2.7.3 SCAPC may be justified where;

(a) expeditious processing of Procurement is necessary;

GOVERNMENT PROCUREMENT GUIDELINES
(b) extraordinary speedy decisions have to be taken for Procurement
of Goods, Services and/or Works;
(c) supplies are immediately required to avoid acute shortages in
the market;
(d) Bids have a very short validity period;
(e) the prices of Goods fluctuate frequently;
(f) items are needed to be purchased very frequently without
significant changes in specifications;
(g) security consideration warrants; and
(h) a project contains a large number of bid packages spread over a
long time span.
